<p>Use this menu to make settings for output tray or to specify how you 
 want to have prints delivered to the output tray.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver 
 you are using.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this menu to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="outputtray" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Output Tray:</span></p>
<p>Specify an output tray. If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Printer 
 Default</span>, prints are delivered to the output tray specified on the 
 printer.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="collate" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Collate:</span></p>
<p>Sorts the prints into sets when multiple sets of documents are printed. 
 Select a collate method in the list.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_COLLATE">Having Prints Sorted</a></p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Printer Collate</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Ignores the application's collate function and applies 
 the printer driver's collate function.</p>
<p aria-level="4" class="T3" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Application Collate</span></p>
<p class="Normal-indent">Applies the collate function set in the application's 
 <span class="Term-OS">Print</span> dialog box.</p>
<p class="Note-indent">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">To apply stacking 
 options, select <span class="Term-Soft">Application Collate</span> and then 
 set the application's collate function to "OFF" in the <span class="Term-OS">Print</span> dialog box.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="collatetype" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Collate Details...</span></p>
<p>Opens the <span class="Term-Soft">Collate Details</span> dialog box, where 
 you can select a collate type.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="mix" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Rotate Mixed Original Orientation...</span></p>
<p>When documents containing a mixture of landscape and portrait pages 
 are printed, document pages whose orientation differs from the paper orientation 
 are rotated by 90 degrees. You can change the direction in which the images 
 are rotated.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="reverse" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Reverse Order Printing</span></p>
<p>When this check box is selected, the document starts printing from the 
 last page. Use this function when prints come out face up in the output 
 tray.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If the application you are using has a similar 
 function, do not make settings with the application's function.</p></li>
<li><p>If you use this function when applying 2 sided 
 printing to a document with an odd number of pages, the blank last page 
 will also be included in the print count.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="faceup" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Eject Face-up</span></p>
<p>Select this to deliver printed documents print side up. Use this function 
 with <span class="Term-Soft">Reverse Order Printing</span> to output a printed 
 document in page order.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/idh_toc_faceup">Printing a Document Face Up</a></p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>This function might not be available depending 
 on the folding type you selected in the <span class="Term-Soft">Fold:</span> 
 list.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="crops" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Print Crop Marks</span></p>
<p>Prints crop marks on each page.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="cropsdetails" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span></p>
<p>Configure settings for crop marks.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="stamp" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Enable [Stamp] in Printer Settings on 
 the Device</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to print stamps registered in the device. If you 
 want to print documents without the stamp, do not click the check box.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>For details about the stamp setting on the device, 
 see the operating instructions provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="2" class="T1" id="insert" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Insert Separation Sheet</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to insert a separation sheet after every set of 
 collated copies. To insert a separator after every two or more sets of 
 copies instead, select the number of sets in the spin box.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span></p>
<p>Select an input tray.</p>
